      "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
      "body": "Concept ACK\n\nThe actual problem in #946 is the intro dialog's prune suggestion (only shown the first time `bitcoin-qt` runs) — `FreespaceChecker` checks datadir's free space but the prune trigger uses the full blockchain + chainstate threshold (~880 GB), incorrectly suggesting prune when `-blocksdir` is set since only ~14 GB of chainstate goes to datadir. Skipping the dialog avoids the wrong suggestion.",
      "user": {
        "login": "pablomartin4btc",
        "id": 110166421,
        "node_id": "U_kgDOBpEBlQ",
        "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/110166421?v=4",
        "gravatar_id": "",
        "url": "https://api.github.com/users/pablomartin4btc",
